    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0492" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/2224: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-12T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 14—8:15
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>37. President Borno reelected President for 4 years by National Assembly this
                    morning by a majority vote of 19 out of 20 present, other vote was a blank.
                    Session was held before the public, including the diplomatic corps, press and
                    many of the candidates.</p>
                <pb facs="0493" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>
                <p>Immediately called on President Borno and congratulated him on his reelection.
                    President Borno stated that he had decided to run for reelection for the sake of
                    continuing [omission?] and that he was prepared to take all risks, even that of
                    assassination.</p>
                <p>Some excitement in the city among the opposition but do not anticipate any
                    serious trouble as the <hi rendition="#italic">gendarmerie</hi> is prepared to
                    handle any that should arise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
